WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.260
While we're still waiting on official confirmation
of the rumor that Charlie Cox's Matt Murdock,

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.910
a.k.a. Daredevil, will appear in the upcoming
third Spider-Man movie as Peter Parker's lawyer,

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:14.519
it seems the fate of one of Cox's co-stars
on Netflix's The Defenders might be starting

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.180
to take shape.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.720
According to We Got This Covered, Marvel brass
may be looking to slot the one and only Luke

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:24.409
Cage into the Marvel Cinematic Universe in
the near future, with the Hero of Harlem reportedly

00:00:24.409 --> 00:00:27.580
set to feature as a prominent supporting player
moving forward.

00:00:27.669 --> 00:00:32.160
The rumor is hardly substantiated, as the
outlet cites an unnamed Marvel insider as

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.630
the source the same who leaked Cox's possible
MCU return in Spider-Man 3.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:40.890
It appears that Marvel Entertainment Chief
Creative Officer Kevin Feige isn't looking

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.240
to simply forget all of the Netflix small-screen
MCU ventures.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:49.051
He's reportedly looking to integrate not only
Daredevil and Luke Cage into the MCU, but

00:00:49.051 --> 00:00:53.960
also Jessica Jones and the Punisher, with
Krysten Ritter and Jon Bernthal both possibly

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.120
reprising their roles.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:59.780
Most surprisingly, the rumor claims that Marvel
isn't interested in bringing actor Mike Colter

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:00.700
back as Cage.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:05.100
The studio is reportedly looking to recast
the role, a fate apparently also shared by

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.520
Iron Fist's Finn Jones.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.899
If these rumors turn out to be true, let's
hope that Marvel finds an actor who can balance

00:01:10.899 --> 00:01:15.350
physicality and emotion as well as Colter
did over his time in the Netflix world of

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.120
the MCU.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:17.960
"Yo, I'm doing the best I can, OK?"

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.440
Marvel is bringing some of its big-screen
heroes to the small screen via Disney+, so

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:26.079
it's not unreasonable to believe that perhaps
the studio wants to blend the heroes of those

00:01:26.079 --> 00:01:29.590
Netflix series into the ever-expanding cinematic
universe.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:34.229
According to Variety, certain legalities between
Marvel and Netflix may prevent any of the

00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:38.929
characters who appeared on those streaming
series from joining in the MCU until at least

00:01:38.929 --> 00:01:41.060
two years after their respective series ended.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:45.880
Daredevil aired its final run of episodes
in October 2018, so it'll be at least another

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.720
year before we see the man without fear in
the MCU.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:52.960
For the Punisher and Jessica Jones, the wait
would be a little longer, as final episodes

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:57.060
of their series aired in January and June
of 2019, respectively.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:01.640
As for a possible timeline on a Luke Cage
return, he was last seen getting cozy in Harlem's

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:07.100
Paradise in June 2018, so it's possible he
could be punching his way back into the MCU

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.120
sooner than any of the other Defenders.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.720
"I don't plan on hibernating.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.560
I was innocent before and I'm innocent now.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:16.180
I got work to do."

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:20.660
Part of the reason these particular characters
made their debuts in small-screen ventures

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:24.660
is because Marvel probably had them marked
as worthy heroes that likely wouldn't have

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.920
drawn huge audiences to theaters in a standalone
movie.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.680
Daredevil's only solo movie venture is not
well-regarded, let's say.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.980
Luke Cage in particular seemed to benefit
from the episodic approach, as well as from

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:40.160
teaming up with other supers in Netflix's
Marvel canon, memorably pairing with both

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.440
Jessica Jones and Iron Fist prior to and after
the Defenders' run.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:49.660
Cage has been one of Marvel Comics' most team-up-friendly
heroes over the years, so if Feige and the

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:54.320
current Marvel crew are eyeing him as a major
supporting player in whatever MCU fun they

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:58.220
might be planning, there's a chance that the
Hero of Harlem could turn up alongside some

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.740
more established supers right out of the gate.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:06.030
Cage's status as an Avenger has been well-established
in the comics, and if the MCU truly is looking

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:10.220
to build its next Avengers big-screen run,
Cage could find himself in the mix when the

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.620
next crossover occurs.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:16.120
We could also see Marvel go the Heroes for
Hire route and deposit Cage in the company

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:19.120
of his Defenders pals Iron Fist and Jessica
Jones.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:23.040
It's also been rumored that Marvel is looking
to bring an alternate super-group into the

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.380
MCU in the near future: The Thunderbolts.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:29.780
And yes, Luke Cage can frequently be seen
fighting alongside that crew, too.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:33.720
So Cage's possible return to the MCU could
take on many different looks.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.720
Could it happen?

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:35.220
Of course.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.860
Might it be an out-and-out farce?

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:37.480
Sure.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.500
Marvel rumors are a dime a dozen.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:42.960
But there's potentially a lot to look forward
to if he does find his way back.

